{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021571-does-anyone-have-any-more-information-about-sulis-as-a-totem","id":1021571,"title":"Does anyone have any more information about Sulis as a totem?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-24T08:04:24-08:00","id":1021571,"title":"Does anyone have any more information about Sulis as a totem?","content":"Hey folks. I was hoping to create a CoG led caern of Healing with Sulis as the totem. Does anyone know of any cultural references about Sulis or where I could find more information? Has anyone used her before? Any non-canon thematic ideas about her? Her write-up is in the Players' Guide Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T10:24:23-08:00","id":1021609,"title":"","content":"Sulis, also Sulis Minerva, is a goddess worshiped at the hot springs of Somerset, England. I used her once and the Caern she was affiliated with had an old roman style bath at it heart. I always had contact with her and offerings to her be through the water at the heart. The water is always warm as if it sits on a natural hot spring even though it does not. When she is angery with the Caern her waters start to go cold until they do something to rectify it.<br /> <br /> For those who petition for her to teach them something, she appears in the water as a woman of average height, build, and appearance with long brown hair half way down her back. She often carries, or has near, an old fashion clay pitcher filled with steaming hot water as if she was just filling the bath. In modern times I used to have her relaxing in the water nude or wearing a very light weight white tunic with a subtle robe around the waste to close the front and back together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T10:44:46-08:00","id":1021616,"title":"","content":"The Celtic deities can be a bit hard to work with since we don't have as strong a record on many of them as we do with many other ancient religions.<br /> <br /> Sulis is one of many that's esp. hard to get into because both the Romans and the Christians reworked her into a fashion that made her more acceptable to their belief structures.<br /> <br /> Sulis can also be a bit weird because she's so associated with Bath now. While her having followers outside of that area is possible, having her be a Caern Totem is kind of like having the City Mother of a different city from where your Sept is as your Caern Totem.<br /> <br /> It might be worth following the Roman take on her. They co-opted Sulis and worked her into Minerva. Minerva's a broader goddess, the Roman's brought her to far more places, and so on. A Caern Totem of Sulis Minerva that focuses on the healer/curse lifter thing helps give you a lot more to work with as aspects of a larger spiritual entity rather than the specific myths that we have around Sulis that's filtered through the Romans at Bath.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T14:40:26-08:00","id":1021701,"title":"","content":"While Sulis is a very specific spirit name, I've always used the totem as the general spirit of any and all thermal springs. Hot mineral springs are seen as therapeutic pretty much everywhere in the world. Rather than try to get specific in terms of the Celtic myths or legends about this one specific deity or spring, I recommend being general. After all, it is Grandfather Thunder and not Jupiter or Thor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T20:14:50-08:00","id":1021780,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wasn't trying to use Sulis as like... *the* Sulis. I was thinking more like the general spirit of thermal springs. I went to her Wiki and she seems pretty awesome. I was actually considering making the caern on a natural hot spring in Virginia. But thanks for everyone's responses!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}